y stylesheet (incl. `@import`) that wasn't served+scanned or can't be read. Refuse `data:`/`blob:` stylesheet URLs at handoff. Base64 regression. |\n| N08 | OPUS-07 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:81-84 | M04 partial: only CSS escapes are decoded; JS `\\x2d`, `\\u002D`, `\\u{2d}` and escaped identifier letters in served JS are not (GPT executed: all returned false), e.g. `setProperty('-webkit-backdrop\\x2dfilter',…)`, `style.webkitBackdrop\\u0046ilter`. | For non-CSS kinds, decode JS escapes before matching; keep CSS handling separate. Regress each form. |\n| N09 | GPT-03 | P2 / P1 | design-probe.mjs:81 | M04 partial: CSS comment stripping `/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g` also runs on JS, so `const a=\"/*\"; el.style.webkitBackdropFilter=\"blur(4px)\"; const b=\"*/\";` returns false (GPT executed; valid JS). | For non-CSS kinds, match both raw and stripped text and fail if either matches (or use language-aware comment handling). Regression with quoted delimiters. |\n| N10 | OPUS-08, GPT-10 | P2 / P2 | scripts/package-r3.py:42,51 | M12 partial: credential stems match only at the start of a path part, and plural `tokens` is allowed with any suffix. GPT executed: `aws-credentials.json`, `client-secret.json`, `client_secrets.json`, `api-token.json`, `github_token.txt`, `prod.secrets.json`, `oauth-tokens.json`, `tokens.production.json`, `tokens.backup.txt` all allowed. | Match stems anywhere at `[._-]` boundaries, plural included. Allow `tokens.json` only per q2 below. Keep the `secret-scan.json` and `token-references.mjs` allowances. Temp-tree tests for inputs and changed paths. |\n| N11 | GPT-04, OPUS-10 | P2 / P2 | integrity.mjs:83; pre-handoff-check.mjs:171-173 | M06 partial: `VECTOR` omits accent ratios (`accentRatio`, `maxViewportAccent`), `filler`, `ruleOfThree`, frames/`unscannedFrames` and `unscannedScopes`; `sum('clipped')` etc. drop width identity, so {1440:1, 320:0} vs {1440:0, 320:1} compare equal. (GPT: lang/dir are already compared via `contentProbe`; Opus's claim