 an internal sideways scroller in one is unmeasured (disclosed as untested, but not gated). | Count closed roots via CDP `DOM.getDocument({pierce:true})` and list them as unscanned scopes that fail at handoff. Regression. |\n| N17 | GPT-11 | P2 / P2 | integrity.mjs:20-34,77 | M13 bypass: the rAF wrapper calls `native.call(window, cb)`, which looks up mutable `Function.prototype.call`; page code can patch it once, capture native rAF, restore it (GPT VM: 101 callbacks, counter stuck at 1, `rafLoopFrom` false). | Bind at init (`Function.prototype.call.bind(native)` or a captured `Reflect.apply`). Add `.call`/`.apply` to `nativeCheck`. Capture-and-restore regression. |\n| N18 | GPT-12, OPUS-13 | P2 / P2 | pre-handoff-check.mjs:222-237 vs 254-267 | M13 incomplete: `rmState` never installs `rafCounterInit`, so a canvas/rAF loop on a declared state is unseen. (Opus also raises an about:blank child-frame rAF timing bypass, UNVERIFIED.) | One hardened reduced-motion routine for the page and every state. Regression: static page plus a state with a rAF loop. Test child-frame coverage separately. |\n| N19 | GPT-13 | ENH / ENH | integrity.mjs:92 | M17 partial: `tamperSigns = []` default treats an omitted native-check result as PASS (the current caller passes null, so this affects the exported API only). | Drop the default; undefined/null → INCOMPLETE. Test. |\n| N20 | OPUS-11, GPT-14 | P2 / P2 | spacing-scale.mjs:27; design-probe.mjs:6-10,64-72; pre-handoff-check.mjs:98-110 | M20/M11 gap: the spacing scan (and its exception registry), type sizes, centred/icon rows, placeholders (`body.innerText`), h1 and the copy TreeWalker skip open shadow roots, so off-scale spacing, lorem ipsum or unlisted copy there pass. | One composed-tree walker for spacingProbe, designProbe counters and copyProbe. Open-shadow regression per check. |\n| N21 | OPUS-12 (GPT MODIFY) | P3 / P3 | release/UNTESTED.md:8,11,22; references/design-quality.md:34 | Docs contradict each other on frames: \"not inspected; a frame is a stop\" vs \"measured with … same-origin frames\" / cross-origin \"blocked\". The truth is partial glass/width inspection of readable frames, plus a mandatory frame FAIL. | Reword to \"partially inspected for glass/width, and every frame fails the handoff\". Mark the R11 wording superseded. Refresh hashes. |\n\n## Disputed — Mi'mar to decide\n| D | Source | Opus | file:line | Opus's point | GPT's rejection |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | OPUS-09 | P2 | spacing-scale.mjs:40-42 | An approved `data-fannan-spacing-exception` excuses any off-scale value, negatives included, so `margin-left:-24px` passes. Fix: never excuse `px < 0`. | The owner rule (ASAD-PANEL-R5:52) refuses negative spacing **tokens**. token-references.mjs:7-16 and token-validation.test.mjs:168-176 deliberately allow negative margins, and scoped exceptions are allowed. A blanket negative-margin ban is a new rule. |\n\n## Panel questions\n**q1 — fail on any frame?**\n- Agreed, 2-0: keep the blanket frame stop for now (now including object/embed/fencedframe, N04). The target is protected recursive scanning of same-origin frames, with unreadable or unsupported frames failing. Switch only once every gate (axe, focus/target size, copy, contrast, spacing, integrity vector, reduced motion) runs inside each frame, because scanning for glass alone would turn \"not checked\" into PASS.\n- Opus adds: real maps and video are usually cross-origin, so the resource boundary already stops them. The design deliverable should be a static poster/placeholder plus an engineering note.\n- Split: Opus wants a scoped, role-reviewed `frameExceptions` entry (screen/state/lang, id, reason, qaGate/approver, manual a11y evidence) in the meantime. GPT says a scoped exception cannot substitute for missing coverage. Mi'mar to decide.\n\n**q2 — plural `tokens` exception?**\n- Agreed, 2-0: **not safe as written**. Allow `tokens.json` only at the declared handoff token path **and** when its content validates as design tokens (DTCG leaves with `$value`; no `access_token`/`refresh_token`/`client_secret` keys). Refuse every other plural, suffixed, prefixed or infixed credential name.\n- Opus adds a stdlib content screen for obvious secrets (`-----BEGIN`, `AKIA…`, `\"refresh_token\"`) on packaged files. GPT agrees it helps but says it can't replace the path+content boundary.\n\n## Verdicts\n- Opus 5.5: round 1 `VERDICT: 13 ISSUES`; after cross-check `VERDICT: 22 ISSUES`.\n- GPT-6.1-Sol: round 1 `VERDICT: 15 ISSUES`; after cross-check `VERDICT: 22 ISSUES`.\n- Merged: 21 agreed (N01-N21) + 1 disputed (D1). Agreed P1 by both: N01, N02. Split P1/lower: N09, N13, N16. **Not zero issues.**\n\n## Cost\nOpus (Claude Code `total_cost_usd`): round 1 $7.04 + cross-check $1.26 = **$8.30** (round 12: $14.39). GPT: no cost reported; tokens 140,126 (round 1) + 68,503 (cross-check). Grok: none (402).\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_014qZqVDGjJtgCvFmACPkdeo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
