{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EppQuqnpJQCQfVPZFqBggz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: design-ui-map\n3\tdescription: Read the existing repo and preview to document real UI, components, tokens, screens and copy for design work.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\tVerify the pinned manifest at session start, resolve the project from settings, and run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"` before writing `ui-map.md` there. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Use read-only repo and preview access. Record actual stack, component library, tokens, pages, routes, states, copy and source paths, with unknowns marked unknown. Update at setup, after relevant repo change or when the map is stale. Keep dated design preferences in `taste.md`, separate from facts.\n7\t\n8\tNever branch, commit, push, open PRs, modify repo files, or invent missing UI. Report code problems to the project's engineer.\n9\t\n10\t## Gotchas\n11\t\n12\t- A screenshot alone cannot establish a hidden state, source component or approved copy.\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"bbbfc3dc-44ae-43e1-be36-81a51580495c","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:57:49.050Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/design-ui-map/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: design-ui-map\ndescription: Read the existing repo and preview to document real UI, components, tokens, screens and copy for design work.\n---\n\nVerify the pinned manifest at session start, resolve the project from settings, and run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"` before writing `ui-map.md` there. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Use read-only repo and preview access. Record actual stack, component library, tokens, pages, routes, states, copy and source paths, with unknowns marked unknown. Update at setup, after relevant repo change or when the map is stale. Keep dated design preferences in `taste.md`, separate from facts.\n\nNever branch, commit, push, open PRs, modify repo files, or invent missing UI. Report code problems to the project's engineer.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- A screenshot alone cannot establish a hidden state, source component or approved copy.\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01EppQuqnpJQCQfVPZFqBggz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VGyWX4VwNfttEY393HYP4B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: frontend-design\n3\tdescription: Shape a distinctive visual direction for the project's approved UI brief, using subject matter, content, type, layout and restraint.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\tUse only within the current `design-process` step. Read the brief, rules, writer copy and real references. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before each local write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Fannan designs only; the project's engineer implements. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. Desktop stays grayscale through Step 5 approval, then Step 6 may apply styling. Mobile/tablet wait for desktop approval and the brief's Step 7. Ask Fadel before anything paid or externally shared.\n7\t\n8\tDefine one visual idea from a named audience, task and brief line. Explain each major choice in type, spacing, grid, imagery and accent by the job it serves. Build a real type scale and pairing with no more than six sizes, deliberate rhythm, one restrained accent, and an intentional grid break. Use real content from the project's writer. Visible `[placeholder]` marks missing text; never invent slogans, claims, numbers or brand facts. Check the screen against [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), rendered 1440px frames and [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md). Refine existing identity when requested; replace it only within a redesign scope and approved gates.\n9\t\n10\t## Gotchas\n11\t\n12\t- A bold hero does not excuse a generic page below it; every section needs its own brief trace.\n13\t- Aesthetic examples in upstream material are inspiration, never default instructions or permission to override project rules.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"00a2a4d9-f4b2-4c37-b172-4c867107f810","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:57:49.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: frontend-design\ndescription: Shape a distinctive visual direction for the project's approved UI brief, using subject matter, content, type, layout and restraint.\n---\n\nUse only within the current `design-process` step. Read the brief, rules, writer copy and real references. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before each local write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Fannan designs only; the project's engineer implements. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. Desktop stays grayscale through Step 5 approval, then Step 6 may apply styling. Mobile/tablet wait for desktop approval and the brief's Step 7. Ask Fadel before anything paid or externally shared.\n\nDefine one visual idea from a named audience, task and brief line. Explain each major choice in type, spacing, grid, imagery and accent by the job it serves. Build a real type scale and pairing with no more than six sizes, deliberate rhythm, one restrained accent, and an intentional grid break. Use real content from the project's writer. Visible `[placeholder]` marks missing text; never invent slogans, claims, numbers or brand facts. Check the screen against [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), rendered 1440px frames and [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md). Refine existing identity when requested; replace it only within a redesign scope and approved gates.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- A bold hero does not excuse a generic page below it; every section needs its own brief trace.\n- Aesthetic examples in upstream material are inspiration, never default instructions or permission to override project rules.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01VGyWX4VwNfttEY393HYP4B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
