{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TGsrMoAz7bFMzVajyLWjbC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: generate-design\n3\tdescription: Generate, edit or vary desktop Stitch screens only when the project selects Stitch and the design stage and approvals allow it.\n4\tallowed-tools:\n5\t  - \"stitch*:*\"\n6\t  - Read\n7\t  - web_fetch\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tUse only when project settings choose Stitch and the pinned manifest check passed. MCP reads `STITCH_API_KEY` from the secret store; never put it in chat, files or a command. Before generation name the Stitch project, exact screens/variants, stage and any cost; obtain Fadel's written yes in Fannan's chat. Ask again before every paid call. No shell, CLI, upload script or repo write. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. A workflow saving local results first runs `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n11\t\n12\tRead the brief, approved screen structure, project rules, writer copy and current design system. Use `list_projects` and `list_design_systems` to identify the correct IDs. Refine a vague request into a precise screen purpose, section structure, real copy, state and 1440px desktop constraint. At Steps 4–5 generate grayscale structure only; color/type generation waits for recorded Step 5 approval. If a project design system exists, let it supply tokens; do not repeat palette/font/roundness instructions in a generation prompt. If none exists, route to `manage-design-system` at the allowed stage. Then choose `generate_screen_from_text`, image-based generation, `edit_screens`, or variant generation as the task requires. Keep the `design-prototype` 3–5 private variant and approver-pick gate. Surface tool suggestions as suggestions, not verified facts. Save named screen/state/version outputs and check [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md) before review.\n13\t\n14\t## Gotchas\n15\t\n16\t- Vendor sample prompts such as glassmorphism or generic card grids are not project direction.\n17\t- Copy, claims, numbers and logos must be confirmed in project files; missing text stays `[placeholder]` and blocks handoff.\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"db03b3c8-6230-4ec8-8318-6d57474f10ef","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:58:07.251Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/generate-design/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: generate-design\ndescription: Generate, edit or vary desktop Stitch screens only when the project selects Stitch and the design stage and approvals allow it.\nallowed-tools:\n  - \"stitch*:*\"\n  - Read\n  - web_fetch\n---\n\nUse only when project settings choose Stitch and the pinned manifest check passed. MCP reads `STITCH_API_KEY` from the secret store; never put it in chat, files or a command. Before generation name the Stitch project, exact screens/variants, stage and any cost; obtain Fadel's written yes in Fannan's chat. Ask again before every paid call. No shell, CLI, upload script or repo write. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. A workflow saving local results first runs `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n\nRead the brief, approved screen structure, project rules, writer copy and current design system. Use `list_projects` and `list_design_systems` to identify the correct IDs. Refine a vague request into a precise screen purpose, section structure, real copy, state and 1440px desktop constraint. At Steps 4–5 generate grayscale structure only; color/type generation waits for recorded Step 5 approval. If a project design system exists, let it supply tokens; do not repeat palette/font/roundness instructions in a generation prompt. If none exists, route to `manage-design-system` at the allowed stage. Then choose `generate_screen_from_text`, image-based generation, `edit_screens`, or variant generation as the task requires. Keep the `design-prototype` 3–5 private variant and approver-pick gate. Surface tool suggestions as suggestions, not verified facts. Save named screen/state/version outputs and check [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md) before review.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Vendor sample prompts such as glassmorphism or generic card grids are not project direction.\n- Copy, claims, numbers and logos must be confirmed in project files; missing text stays `[placeholder]` and blocks handoff.\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01TGsrMoAz7bFMzVajyLWjbC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
