{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I have enough to start Part B findings now while the agent continues running. The seven-state interaction model (default, hover, focus, disabled, empty, loading, error) is missing several important states like success, active/pressed, selected, visited, read-only, skeleton loading, and permission-denied scenarios - this gap belongs in the handoff contract issue.\n\nBeyond that, there's no form design or UX writing guidance at all for a UI/UX bot - no coverage of error message content requirements, label vs placeholder conventions, validation timing, or helper text standards. That's a core gap worth splitting into forms guidance (P1, since desktop UIs rely heavily on forms) and microcopy guidance (P2).\n\nThe research/discovery process also looks thin: design-research only covers reference craft, with no user research methods, competitive audits, analytics evidence, or assumption logging. The testing step mentions recording tasks but gives no actual protocol for task scenarios, success criteria, or participant counts.\n\nThen I'm cataloguing IA gaps (no navigation model, wayfinding, or content priority structure), flow spec gaps (missing entry points, decision points, error paths), visual hierarchy gaps (no squint test, scanning patterns, single-primary-action rule), typography gaps (measure, line-height, minimum size, Arabic-specific rules), and colour system gaps (tonal scales, state colour derivation, semantic tokens, focus ring contrast) — each landing around P2 severity.\n\nI also notice a direct contradiction: the frontend-design skill mandates an \"intentional grid break,\" which conflicts with the plan's instruction not to fabricate irregularity — that's a concrete P2 defect, alongside missing grid/gutter defaults and no rule for ultrawide desktop widths beyond 1440. Then I start flagging that components lack a proper spec template covering anatomy and variants.\n\nChecking the a11y audit skill against WCAG items, several are missing from its checklist: text spacing (1.4.12), content on hover/focus (1.4.13), error identification/suggestion (3.3.1/3.3.3), error prevention (3.3.4), input purpose autocomplete (1.3.5), label in name (2.5.3), status messages (4.1.3), and forced-colors support — flagging as P2 since some overlap with existing \"errors\" coverage. Also noting there's no defined protocol for capturing Fadel's feedback during iteration cycles.\n\nI'm checking the critique rubric too — it has 8 rows scored 0-4 with a stopping threshold, but lacks a Nielsen heuristics pass and consistency checks, though critic independence seems adequately defined as a separate read-only reviewer.\n\nNo redline spec covers responsive behavior between desktop widths or interaction edge cases like long names, zero/one/many items, and truncation policy; data extremes testing only covers copy stress, not user-generated data variations. Data-heavy desktop UIs (tables, dashboards) also lack guidance on numeric alignment, sticky headers, sort/filter states, density modes, and bulk actions — flagging both as P2 gaps.\n\nI'm reviewing the design-process skill's discovery step, which skips gathering existing analytics, support data, and constraints — this should merge into the earlier gap about product context. The grayscale/no-styling guidance and the critic-rubric stopping rule both seem fine as written. For priority levels, I'm leaning toward keeping forms and error-content design as the one P1 since missing guidance there risks shipping amateur-looking placeholder-as-label patterns, while usability testing protocols and missing success states stay at P2.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_8d56e8f163fc4277ae557426cd8ad783","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":20501,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"e04eb792-e727-4e80-8974-1689457ac55c","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:58:41.217Z","thinking_duration_ms":27796,"thinking_display":"updates"}
