{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012FzhMe6Xn2CEQ41G6gPKJ4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: impeccable\n3\tdescription: Inspect local UI mockups for visual, usability and accessibility issues using only the reviewed read-only detector.\n4\tallowed-tools:\n5\t  - Read\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\tUse for a focused design critique after the current step permits rendered mockups. Verify the pinned manifest at session start. The reviewed `pre-handoff-check.mjs` invokes the pinned launcher on local files inside `/workspace/design-output/<project>/`; inspect its resulting evidence. The launcher permits `--version` and `detect` with reviewed flags; `IMPECCABLE_BIN` must point to the pinned binary and `FANNAN_PROJECT` must identify the selected project; detect paths must stay inside that project's output folder. The launcher passes a minimal environment to the copied executable, never the caller's keys. Do not invoke the binary or an alternate CLI directly. No `npx`, live mode, generate, install, update, hooks, doctor, context or repo mutation. The workflow runs `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"` before saving a finding. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n9\t\n10\tRead the brief, approved structure, DESIGN.md, writer copy and [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md). Use detection to find hierarchy, contrast, type, alignment, state and copy problems; inspect real screenshots at 1440px and report evidence with severity. Detection is advisory and cannot waive the [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md), WCAG 2.2 AA or a recorded approval. The design itself remains in the project's output folder; Fannan never edits the repo.\n11\t\n12\t## Gotchas\n13\t\n14\t- If the launcher or hash check fails, report the blocked detector; do not call the binary directly.\n15\t- Detector findings are neither proof of accessibility compliance nor permission to enter the next design step.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"6e05953f-3a64-4719-a960-861599cff659","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:58:41.233Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/impeccable/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: impeccable\ndescription: Inspect local UI mockups for visual, usability and accessibility issues using only the reviewed read-only detector.\nallowed-tools:\n  - Read\n---\n\nUse for a focused design critique after the current step permits rendered mockups. Verify the pinned manifest at session start. The reviewed `pre-handoff-check.mjs` invokes the pinned launcher on local files inside `/workspace/design-output/<project>/`; inspect its resulting evidence. The launcher permits `--version` and `detect` with reviewed flags; `IMPECCABLE_BIN` must point to the pinned binary and `FANNAN_PROJECT` must identify the selected project; detect paths must stay inside that project's output folder. The launcher passes a minimal environment to the copied executable, never the caller's keys. Do not invoke the binary or an alternate CLI directly. No `npx`, live mode, generate, install, update, hooks, doctor, context or repo mutation. The workflow runs `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"` before saving a finding. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n\nRead the brief, approved structure, DESIGN.md, writer copy and [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md). Use detection to find hierarchy, contrast, type, alignment, state and copy problems; inspect real screenshots at 1440px and report evidence with severity. Detection is advisory and cannot waive the [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md), WCAG 2.2 AA or a recorded approval. The design itself remains in the project's output folder; Fannan never edits the repo.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- If the launcher or hash check fails, report the blocked detector; do not call the binary directly.\n- Detector findings are neither proof of accessibility compliance nor permission to enter the next design step.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_012FzhMe6Xn2CEQ41G6gPKJ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
