{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"The proxy seems fine for context() calls. I'm confirming shadow root piercing works correctly with DOM.getDocument, filtering out user-agent shadow roots while cross-origin frames remain excluded regardless since they fail independently. Now I'm turning to how sheets get listed for a given target.\n\nFor a blocked @import, the question is whether the sheet reference ends up null or an empty stylesheet object — either way, a blocked network request fails the resource boundary check anyway, so unserved and blocked collapse into the same failure case. I'm also considering whether file:// URLs count as readable or cross-origin given Chrome's unique-origin treatment of file schemes.\n\nAccessing cssRules on a file:// linked sheet can throw a SecurityError, which explains why the served check is necessary; I'm assuming the sheet's href normalizes the same way as the request URL. For `data:` or `blob:` stylesheet references, whether via link tags, @import, or object URLs, these get refused outright since they're not routed. Frames fail by default, inline `<style>` elements are scanned via textContent since they have no href, and shadow DOM stylesheets are already covered through shadowRoot.styleSheets — though I notice the recursive handling of nested imports contradicts earlier documentation claiming only one level is supported.\n\nNow I'm worried about a stylesheet served with an incorrect MIME type — if a .css file is served with a non-matching extension like .txt and comes back as text/plain, it gets added to the served set but scanGlass skips it since the content-type regex won't match, meaning it never gets scanned for glass despite potentially being applied by the browser anyway.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_63c6af478c3e4cf1a9ca780704f6c9f2","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":11806,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DPkzkRuJaRjVw8TvQQyMje","agent_id":"ab187913895d29e5f","session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"067dc19a-1beb-4c6f-98e2-e8c4af9673de","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:59:00.362Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Part A gate diff review"}
