{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TWujstTgihuwwhxU7ADMPD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { readFileSync, realpathSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\n2\timport { extname, sep } from 'node:path';\n3\timport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n4\t\n5\tconst types = { '.html': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', '.css': 'text/css; charset=utf-8', '.js': 'text/javascript; charset=utf-8', '.json': 'application/json', '.png': 'image/png', '.jpg': 'image/jpeg', '.jpeg': 'image/jpeg', '.svg': 'image/svg+xml', '.woff': 'font/woff', '.woff2': 'font/woff2' };\n6\texport function localAsset(url, projectRoot) {\n7\t  const parsed = new URL(url);\n8\t  if (parsed.protocol !== 'file:' || parsed.search || parsed.hash) throw Error('only local project files are allowed');\n9\t  const root = realpathSync(projectRoot), path = realpathSync(fileURLToPath(parsed));\n10\t  if (!path.startsWith(root + sep) || !statSync(path).isFile()) throw Error('file request is outside the selected project');\n11\t  const contentType = types[extname(path).toLowerCase()];\n12\t  if (!contentType) throw Error('file type is not allowed');\n13\t  return { body: readFileSync(path), contentType, path };\n14\t}\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DPkzkRuJaRjVw8TvQQyMje","agent_id":"ab187913895d29e5f","session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"503f9e06-0f4c-4889-8342-e2365a01989b","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:59:00.387Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01TWujstTgihuwwhxU7ADMPD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Part A gate diff review"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm checking that .mjs files aren't allowed, confirming the glass check scans served files via CSSOM, and verifying the shared `served` set works correctly across jsOff and other contexts, including how closedShadowRoots and readable sheets factor into integrity checks.\n\nOne gap I'm finding: @import rules in CSSOM only expose the import statement itself, not the imported sheet's contents, so nested imported sheets aren't glass-scanned through sheetGlass directly — but this is covered since served files get raw byte scanning separately, including imports inside `<style>` elements. Grouping rules like @media handle nested content fine since their cssText includes inner rules. I'm also confirming constructed sheets and `<style>` elements with no href are treated as readable, and noting that shadow-root `<link>` stylesheets and their @import chains are included but currently untested, which I should flag.\n\nI'm uncertain whether Chrome treats file:// stylesheets as cross-origin, blocking cssRules access — that would affect whether data:/blob: imports inside served sheets get properly refused per N07. I'll flag this as P2 conditional, pending verification of file:// sheet readability.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_c729feb92bf3414ab3b00fb3f53a1069","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":11824,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DPkzkRuJaRjVw8TvQQyMje","agent_id":"ab187913895d29e5f","session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"27810626-cd95-41f9-ad4a-d44bd34981bc","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:59:18.512Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Part A gate diff review"}
