{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm noting that even though the sheet reads as readable with no glass effect, Chrome strips the backdrop-filter property at parse time, meaning the refusal logic must rely on checking the href itself rather than the parsed CSS. Testing whether a data URI imported via @import inside a style element also gets caught by that href check.\n\nBut a deeper concern: for served file:// stylesheets, Chrome may throw a SecurityError when accessing cssRules since each local file is treated as a unique origin, so listSheet's recursion into @import rules might fail silently on those — I need to check whether Playwright's route fulfillment preserves that cross-origin restriction given the isolated world's access settings.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_224dbdd9780e4d878f2e44f17c5853f0","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":11914,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DPkzkRuJaRjVw8TvQQyMje","agent_id":"ab187913895d29e5f","session_id":"f0bd072d-d495-4454-a967-3e00aaf8b556","uuid":"eb8e1751-0f07-4508-8f24-5b3619f5b59a","timestamp":"2026-10-18T02:59:49.485Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Part A gate diff review"}
